  "worked_solution": "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules to the given sum, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{70}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{80}2({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & =2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{70}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{80}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) \\\\  & =2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{70}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{80}{a}_{ij}+2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{70}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{80}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 75+2\\cdot 70 \\\\  & =150+140 \\\\  & =290.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
